Components derived from other models
------------------------------------

Hector ocean carbon model (scm4opt/physics/ocean_hector.py)
  Ported from the four-box ocean of Hector v1.0, https://github.com/JGCRI/hector,
  licensed under the GNU General Public License v3.0.
  Hartin, C. A., Patel, P., Schwarber, A., Link, R. P., and Bond-Lamberty, B. P. (2015):
  A simple object-oriented and open-source model for scientific and policy analyses of the
  global climate system - Hector v1.0. Geosci. Model Dev., 8, 939-955,
  doi:10.5194/gmd-8-939-2015.

OSCAR (scm4opt/physics/ocean_oscar.py and parts of scm4opt/physics/chemistry.py)
  The mixed-layer ocean carbon model and the OH / photolysis sink formulations follow
  OSCAR v2, https://github.com/tgasser/OSCAR, distributed under the CeCILL Free Software
  License Agreement v2.1, which permits distribution under the GNU GPL (Art. 5.3.4).
  Gasser, T., Ciais, P., Boucher, O., Quilcaille, Y., Tortora, M., Bopp, L., and
  Hauglustaine, D. (2017): The compact Earth system model OSCAR v2.2: description and first
  results. Geosci. Model Dev., 10, 271-319, doi:10.5194/gmd-10-271-2017.

DOECLIM energy-balance model (scm4opt/physics/doeclim.py)
  Kriegler, E. (2005): Imprecise probability analysis for integrated assessment of climate
  change. PhD thesis, University of Potsdam.
  Tanaka, K. and Kriegler, E. (2007): Aggregated carbon cycle, atmospheric chemistry, and
  climate model (ACC2) - description of the forward and inverse modes. Reports on Earth
  System Science 40, Max Planck Institute for Meteorology, Hamburg.

MAGICC6 (scm4opt/physics/land.py structure; scm4opt/data/MAGICC6/)
  The land carbon-cycle formulation follows MAGICC6. The parameter values of the
  MAGICC6-defaults mode are in scm4opt/data/MAGICC6/land_c4mip_bern.csv; they come from the
  configuration files distributed with the MAGICC6 executable and are NOT covered by the
  GNU GPL: they are licensed by T. Wigley, S. Raper and M. Meinshausen under the Creative
  Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 3.0 Unported License
  (scm4opt/data/MAGICC6/NOTICE.txt).
  Meinshausen, M., Raper, S. C. B., and Wigley, T. M. L. (2011): Emulating coupled
  atmosphere-ocean and carbon cycle models with a simpler model, MAGICC6 - Part 1: Model
  description and calibration. Atmos. Chem. Phys., 11, 1417-1456,
  doi:10.5194/acp-11-1417-2011.

SCM4OPT was developed from the climate module of AD-DICE2013R (DICE-2013R, W. Nordhaus).


Data
----

The files in scm4opt/data/ other than scm4opt/data/MAGICC6/ are input data and parameter
tables. The scenario inputs (RCMIP3/, contrib/, AGAGE/, NOAA/) are derived from external
datasets (RCMIP, CEDS, LUH2, AGAGE, NOAA and others) and remain subject to the terms and
citation requirements of those datasets.
